IMPORT prelude

-- Housing Act 1980 (Western Australia) -- what the Housing Authority may do for a person who wants to buy or rent a home:
-- applications (s 15), the "eligible person" (s 5(2), (3)), loans (ss 35-42), guarantees and interest subsidies (ss 46,
-- 47), letting houses and their rent (ss 28-31), selling houses and housing land on terms (ss 32-34), specialised housing
-- (s 60), more time to pay in hardship (s 68), and paying duty and fees and adding them to the debt (ss 72, 73).
--
-- SEAT: the low-income home buyer (a Keystart or shared-equity buyer) and the public housing tenant, asking "Can the
-- Housing Authority help me buy or rent?". The Act is constitutive: almost every operative provision says what the
-- Authority MAY do ("may make a loan", "may let or lease", "may assist him by guarantee", "may credit"). It gives the person
-- no entitlement; the one duty owed to an applicant is s 15(1), that the Authority "shall deal with" the application. So
-- each decision here answers "does the Act let the Authority do this for me?", and a TRUE means the power exists, never that
-- it will be used. Who is an "eligible person" is not in the Act: s 5(2) leaves it to "conditions of eligibility from time
-- to time determined by the Authority and approved by the Minister", by reference to income (s 5(3)). Those conditions,
-- the Minister's gazetted limits (ss 34, 40, 46(2)(a)), the gazetted standard interest rates (ss 33(4), 42(1)), the rent
-- determinations (s 30) and Keystart's lending policy are policy, not law, and are asked as inputs. Judgments the Act hands
-- to the Authority or the Minister ("in the opinion of the Authority", "satisfies the Authority", "with the consent of the
-- Minister", "in cases of hardship") are asked as facts, never guessed.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 5(2), (3); s 15(1); s 28; s 30; s 31(1), (2); s 32; s 33(1), (6); s 34(1); s 35; s 36(1);
-- s 37; s 38(1), (3); s 40(1); s 41(1); s 42(3); s 46(1), (2)(a); s 47(1), (2); s 60(1)(a), (b); s 68; s 72; s 73.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 37092, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_37092.txt; its compilation table runs to the Public Health (Consequential Provisions)
-- Act 2016 (Reprint 4 as at 2 September 2016 is the last reprint listed). No regulations or gazetted determinations were
-- deposited or used: the eligibility conditions, the Minister's limits, the standard rates of interest and the rent
-- determinations are inputs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Authority's constitution, management, staff, directions and delegation (Part II, ss 6-14, 16-18A);
-- land acquisition and development and the power to lease or sell land other than houses (Part III Division 1, Division 2
-- ss 19-27); the Commonwealth arrangements (Part V Division 1) and the State's loan agreements with lending institutions
-- (Part V Division 2, ss 52-59), save that the person's position under them is answered by `What does the Housing Act
-- decide about my loan from`; community facilities (s 61); Aboriginal housing management agreements (Part VA, ss 62A-62M);
-- funds and borrowing (ss 62-65); regulations (ss 70, 71); transitional provisions (Part IX). The tenancy itself (beyond
-- s 28-31) is governed by the Residential Tenancies Act 1987, encoded separately.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the low-income home buyer and public housing tenant,
-- with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
-- Not for public use as advice.

§ `Housing Act 1980 (WA) -- can the Housing Authority help me buy or rent`

§§ `the person and the facts`

-- s 5(2): "A reference in a provision of this Act to an eligible person is a reference to a person who satisfies the
-- conditions of eligibility from time to time determined by the Authority and approved by the Minister for the purposes of
-- that provision." s 5(3): the conditions "shall be determined and approved by reference to income criteria".
-- s 32(2), s 35: a "house" in Divisions 4 (sale) and Part IV Division 1 (loans) is one "intended to be used by the
-- purchaser [or borrower] as a home for himself and his family (if any)". s 5(1) "house" includes "any single, attached or
-- multistorey dwelling unit", so an apartment is a house.
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the house is to be a home for me and my family` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 36(1)(a)-(e), s 37, s 38(1): the purposes for which Part IV Division 1 lets the Authority lend.
DECLARE `Purpose of the loan` IS ONE OF
    `to build, finish, enlarge or improve a house on land I own`
    `to buy land and build a house on it`
    `to buy a house and its land`
    `to buy a partly built house and its land and finish it`
    `to pay off a mortgage on my land where a house is or will be`
    `to buy land from the Authority to build a house on`
    `to alter or add to my house to meet local laws or for comfort`
    `some other purpose`

-- Divisions 3 and 4 of Part III deal with houses and housing land "held by the Authority" (s 5(1A)(c), (d)).
DECLARE `What the Authority would sell me` IS ONE OF
    `a house and land held by the Authority`
    `land held by the Authority, to build a house on`
    `something not held by the Authority`

DECLARE `Terms of sale` IS ONE OF
    `for cash or on terms of payment the Authority thinks fit`
    `for cash only`
    `not a sale under Division 4`

-- Who would be lending. Keystart is not named anywhere in the Act.
DECLARE Lender IS ONE OF
    `the Housing Authority under Part IV`
    `Keystart or another company`
    `a lender approved for an interest subsidy under s 47`
    `a lending institution under a State loan agreement`

§§ `s 15 -- my application`

-- s 15(1): "The Authority shall deal with applications for housing or financial assistance for housing made under this Act
-- ...". s 15(2): it may inquire, require further information, require it "to be verified by statutory declaration",
-- approve "wholly or in part" or refuse.
@export Must the Housing Authority deal with my application (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 15(1))?
GIVEN `I am applying for housing or financial help for housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application is for housing or for financial assistance for housing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Housing Authority deal with my application` `I am applying for housing or financial help for housing` IF
    `I am applying for housing or financial help for housing`

§§ `ss 35-38 -- can the Authority lend to me`

-- s 36(1): "Subject to this Act the Authority may make a loan to any eligible person in order to assist the eligible person
-- -- (a) to erect, complete, enlarge or improve a house on land owned by him; or (b) to purchase land and erect a house
-- thereon; or (c) to purchase a house and the land on which it is erected; or (d) to purchase a partially erected house ...
-- and complete the house; or (e) to discharge any mortgage or liability already existing on land owned by him ...".
-- s 37: "the Authority may make a loan to any person in order to assist the person to purchase from the Authority land on
-- which to erect a house". s 38(1): a loan "to any person" for alterations or additions to bring a house into conformity
-- with local laws or the Water Services Act 2012 "or to improve the standard of comfort or convenience of the house";
-- s 38(3): only to "a person who satisfies the Authority that his financial position justifies the assistance".
-- s 35: in this Division a house is one "used by the person to whom the loan is to be made as a home for himself and his
-- family (if any)".
@export Can the Housing Authority lend me money for this purpose under the Housing Act 1980 (WA) Part IV (ss 35-38)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Whether you meet the Authority's eligibility conditions, and whether the house is to be your home
      `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of the loan` @desc What the loan is for
      `the Authority is satisfied my financial position justifies the help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an alteration loan only (s 38(3)): the Authority's judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this` `me` `the purpose` `the Authority is satisfied my financial position justifies the help` IF
        `me`'s `the house is to be a home for me and my family`
    AND (CONSIDER `the purpose`
         WHEN `to buy land from the Authority to build a house on` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to alter or add to my house to meet local laws or for comfort` THEN `the Authority is satisfied my financial position justifies the help`
         WHEN `some other purpose` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE `me`'s `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)`)

-- s 40(1): "The total amount lent to a person under this Division and for the time being remaining owing shall not exceed
-- such sum as is determined by the Minister ... by notice published in the Government Gazette." s 73(2): fees and duty
-- added under s 73(1) may take the balance over that sum. The gazetted sum is not deposited and is an input.
@export Would this new loan keep what I owe the Housing Authority within the Minister's limit (s 40(1), s 73(2))?
GIVEN `what I owe now under Part IV, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the new loan` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area and purpose` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would this loan keep me within the Minister's limit` `what I owe now under Part IV, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` `the new loan` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area and purpose` IF
    (`what I owe now under Part IV, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` PLUS `the new loan`) AT MOST `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area and purpose`

-- s 41(1): repayment "shall be secured by -- (a) a first or second mortgage in an approved form to the Authority, of the
-- borrower's estate and interest in the land ...; and (b) such additional or collateral security (if any) as to the
-- Authority may seem fit".
@export What security must I give for a Housing Authority loan (s 41(1))?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What security must I give for a Part IV loan` IS
    "a first or second mortgage to the Authority over the land and its improvements, and any further security the Authority requires"

-- s 42(3): the interest rate in the mortgage "shall be the standard rate of interest most recently published under
-- subsection (1) in respect of loans of that class", and may vary with later determinations. s 33(6) says the same of a
-- contract of sale on terms. The gazetted rates are not deposited and are an input.
@export What interest rate will my Housing Authority loan or contract of sale on terms carry (ss 33(6), 42(3))?
GIVEN `the standard rate most recently gazetted for this class` IS A NUMBER @desc Percent a year (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What interest rate will I pay` `the standard rate most recently gazetted for this class` IS
    `the standard rate most recently gazetted for this class`

§§ `ss 46, 47 -- guarantees and interest subsidies`

-- s 46(1): "Where an eligible person desires to -- (a) erect a house; or (b) complete a partially erected house; or (c)
-- purchase a new house, and is able without borrowing to pay so much of the cost ... as the Authority approves but is unable
-- to borrow, without assistance under this section from the Authority, sufficient money in order to enable him to pay the
-- balance of the cost, the Authority may assist him by guarantee". s 46(2)(a): the house must be a home for him and his
-- family and its value "(exclusive of the value of the land ...)" must not exceed the sum the Minister gazettes. "New house"
-- takes its meaning from the Housing Loan Guarantee Act 1957 s 3 (repealed; note 3 to the compilation), asked as a fact.
@export Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing to build, finish or buy a new home (s 46)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Your eligibility and whether the house is to be your home
      `I want to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 46(1)(a)-(c)
      `I can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Your deposit
      `I cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether lenders will lend you the rest unaided
      `the value of the house, not counting the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing` `me` `I want to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house` `I can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves` `I cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee` `the value of the house, not counting the land` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here` IF
        `me`'s `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)`
    AND `me`'s `the house is to be a home for me and my family`
    AND `I want to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house`
    AND `I can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves`
    AND `I cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee`
    AND `the value of the house, not counting the land` AT MOST `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here`

-- s 47(1): to assist eligible persons "by subsidising the rate or amounts of interest payable in respect of loans made to
-- them by approved lending institutions, the Authority may, with the approval of the Minister -- (a) make payments ... to
-- approved lending institutions that make loans to approved persons on the security of freehold or leasehold property by
-- way of mortgage". s 47(2): "approved lending institution" is one "approved in writing by the Minister"; "approved person
-- means an eligible person approved in writing by the Authority".
@export Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my home loan (s 47)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Your eligibility
      `the Authority has approved me in writing for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(2) "approved person"
      `my lender is approved in writing by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(2) "approved lending institution"
      `my loan is secured by a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On freehold or leasehold property
      `the Minister approves the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan` `me` `the Authority has approved me in writing for this` `my lender is approved in writing by the Minister` `my loan is secured by a mortgage` `the Minister approves the payments` IF
        `me`'s `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)`
    AND `the Authority has approved me in writing for this`
    AND `my lender is approved in writing by the Minister`
    AND `my loan is secured by a mortgage`
    AND `the Minister approves the payments`

-- Keystart and the Part V Division 2 loan agreements. The Act does not mention Keystart. s 12(b), (d) give the Authority
-- the powers of a private person and the power "to borrow and lend money", "subject to and for the purposes of this Act";
-- s 12A lets it enter joint ventures with the Minister's approval. Neither sets terms a borrower could rely on. s 54(2)(c),
-- (d): a State loan agreement may prohibit the institution from lending where the home's value or the borrower's income
-- exceeds amounts the Minister determines; those are terms between the State and the institution, not the borrower.
@export What does the Housing Act 1980 (WA) itself decide about my home loan from this lender?
GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender @desc Who is lending to you
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What does the Housing Act decide about my loan from` `the lender` IS
    CONSIDER `the lender`
    WHEN `the Housing Authority under Part IV` THEN "the purposes, the Minister's limit, the mortgage and the gazetted rate (ss 35-42); eligibility is the Authority's policy"
    WHEN `Keystart or another company` THEN "nothing: the Act does not name Keystart; its lending policy is not law and is an input"
    WHEN `a lender approved for an interest subsidy under s 47` THEN "only whether the Authority may subsidise the interest (s 47); the loan terms are the lender's"
    OTHERWISE "nothing directly: value and income caps in a State loan agreement bind the institution, not me (s 54(2))"

§§ `ss 28-31 -- renting a house from the Authority`

-- s 28: "The Authority may let or lease any house or house and land held by the Authority to any eligible person or, with
-- the consent of the Minister -- (a) to any public authority or body corporate; or (b) to any person who, in the opinion of
-- the Authority, is providing an essential community or tradesman service in a locality and is unable to obtain suitable
-- accommodation in that locality from any source other than the Authority."
@export Can the Housing Authority rent me one of its houses (s 28)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Your eligibility for public housing
      `the Authority thinks I provide an essential community or tradesman service here and cannot find suitable accommodation elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 28(b): the Authority's opinion
      `the Minister consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 28: needed for a person who is not eligible
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Housing Authority rent me a house` `me` `the Authority thinks I provide an essential community or tradesman service here and cannot find suitable accommodation elsewhere` `the Minister consents` IF
        `me`'s `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)`
    OR  (    `the Minister consents`
         AND `the Authority thinks I provide an essential community or tradesman service here and cannot find suitable accommodation elsewhere`)

-- s 30(1): the rent is "such amounts as are from time to time determined by the Authority and approved by the Minister";
-- s 30(2)(c): a determination may provide for "the allowance of rebates in such circumstances and subject to such conditions
-- as are specified in the determination". The determination is not deposited and is an input.
@export How much rent must I pay the Housing Authority (s 30)?
GIVEN `the rent determined for my house and my class of tenant` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars a week, from the Authority's determination
      `the rebate the determination allows me` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars a week
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much rent must I pay` `the rent determined for my house and my class of tenant` `the rebate the determination allows me` IS
    IF `the rebate the determination allows me` AT LEAST `the rent determined for my house and my class of tenant`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the rent determined for my house and my class of tenant` MINUS `the rebate the determination allows me`

-- s 31(1): where the purchaser of a house and land under Division 4, or the purchaser's "spouse, de facto partner or
-- deceased spouse or deceased de facto partner", has been a tenant of it under Division 3, "the Authority may credit towards
-- the purchase price ... the rents that have been paid ... or such portion (if any) of those rents as the Authority thinks
-- fit". s 31(2): an option to purchase in the tenancy agreement keeps its own crediting terms. s 31(3): rents include
-- amounts the tenant paid for repair, renovation, upkeep or improvement.
@export Can the rent I (or my partner) paid be credited towards buying the house from the Housing Authority (s 31)?
GIVEN `I am buying the house and land from the Authority under Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 31(1)
      `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 31(1)(a), (b)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my rent be credited towards the price` `I am buying the house and land from the Authority under Division 4` `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority` IF
        `I am buying the house and land from the Authority under Division 4`
    AND `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority`

§§ `ss 32-34 -- buying a house or land from the Authority`

-- s 32(1): Division 4 "applies to the sale by the Authority of a house and land held by the Authority or land held by the
-- Authority on which a house is to be erected"; s 32(2): the house is one "intended to be used by the purchaser as a home
-- for himself and his family (if any)". s 33(1): the Authority may sell "(a) for cash; or (b) in the case of -- (i) the
-- sale of land; or (ii) the sale of a house and land to an eligible person, on such terms of payment as the Authority
-- thinks fit". A sale outside Division 4 is under s 26 (with the Minister's consent, cash or terms), not encoded.
@export On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me a home (ss 32, 33(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Your eligibility, and whether it is to be your home
      `what is for sale` IS A `What the Authority would sell me` @desc What the Authority would sell
GIVETH A `Terms of sale`
DECIDE `On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this` `me` `what is for sale` IS
    IF (NOT `me`'s `the house is to be a home for me and my family`)
    THEN `not a sale under Division 4`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what is for sale`
         WHEN `something not held by the Authority` THEN `not a sale under Division 4`
         WHEN `land held by the Authority, to build a house on` THEN `for cash or on terms of payment the Authority thinks fit`
         OTHERWISE IF `me`'s `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)`
                   THEN `for cash or on terms of payment the Authority thinks fit`
                   ELSE `for cash only`

-- s 34(1): "The balance of the purchase money for the time being remaining unpaid under a contract of sale ... under this
-- Division shall not exceed such sum as is determined by the Minister ... by notice published in the Government Gazette."
-- s 73(2) lets added fees and duty exceed it.
@export Would the unpaid price under my contract with the Housing Authority stay within the Minister's limit (s 34(1))?
GIVEN `the unpaid balance, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would the unpaid price stay within the Minister's limit` `the unpaid balance, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area` IF
    `the unpaid balance, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` AT MOST `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area`

§§ `s 60 -- specialised housing`

-- s 60(1)(a), (b): the Authority may provide and let units in "specialized housing for the purpose of housing persons,
-- including students and aged and infirm persons, whose housing requirements are not, in the opinion of the Authority,
-- otherwise adequately provided for under the provisions of this Act". No eligibility condition is stated.
@export Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing such as student or aged housing (s 60)?
GIVEN `the Authority thinks my housing needs are not otherwise adequately provided for under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 60(1)(a): the Authority's opinion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing` `the Authority thinks my housing needs are not otherwise adequately provided for under the Act` IF
    `the Authority thinks my housing needs are not otherwise adequately provided for under the Act`

§§ `ss 68, 72, 73 -- paying the Authority`

-- s 68: "The Authority may, in cases of hardship, extend the due date for the payment of any moneys payable to the Authority
-- by a purchaser, tenant, mortgagor or other debtor, for such time, and upon such terms and conditions, as the Authority with
-- the approval of the Minister may determine." Whether it is a case of hardship is the Authority's call, asked as a fact.
@export Can the Housing Authority give me more time to pay what I owe it (s 68)?
GIVEN `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 68
      `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Authority's judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be given more time to pay the Authority` `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor` `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship` IF
        `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor`
    AND `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship`

-- s 72: "The Authority may pay registration fees and duty under the Duties Act 2008 in relation to a sale made under
-- Division 4 of Part III or a loan made under Division 1 of Part IV on behalf of the person ... and may recover the amount so
-- paid from him." s 73(1): it may add those amounts, and application, valuation and document fees, to the balance owing,
-- (2) even beyond the s 34 or s 40 limit.
@export Can the Housing Authority pay my stamp duty and registration fees and add them to what I owe (ss 72, 73)?
GIVEN `my purchase or loan is a Division 4 sale or a Part IV loan from the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Not a loan from Keystart or a bank
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Authority pay my duty and add it to what I owe` `my purchase or loan is a Division 4 sale or a Part IV loan from the Authority` IF
    `my purchase or loan is a Division 4 sale or a Part IV loan from the Authority`
